{"format":"tvf-scene","v":1,"name":"example · where it shows up","loop":48,"ease":"inout","hold":0,"gravity":1,"wind":0,"trail":null,"camera":[{"t":0,"box":[-0.517483984,-0.0628333714,0.0399329633,0.0789231673]},{"t":0.02,"box":[-0.366612245,-0.026522449,-0.110938776,0.0420979614]},{"t":0.35,"box":[-0.366612245,-0.0506939395,-0.110938776,0.0420979614]},{"t":0.4,"box":[-0.409929796,-0.0385420448,-0.0676212245,0.0428032675]},{"t":0.52,"box":[-0.409929796,-0.0385420448,-0.0676212245,0.0428032675]},{"t":0.57,"box":[0.183820408,-0.0512816327,0.293730612,0.0586285714]},{"t":0.625,"box":[0.183820408,-0.0512816327,0.293730612,0.0586285714]},{"t":0.68,"box":[0.158102141,-0.121022745,0.31944888,0.128369682]},{"t":0.75,"box":[0.158102141,-0.121022745,0.31944888,0.128369682]},{"t":0.79,"box":[0.419364147,-0.0802203429,0.535737894,0.0655338122]},{"t":0.9,"box":[0.419364147,-0.0802203429,0.535737894,0.0655338122]},{"t":0.95,"box":[-0.352912776,-0.145468288,0.563277673,0.152815225]}],"stops":[0.17,0.35,0.52,0.75,0.9],"beats":[{"title":"A lamp turns over a straight shore","text":"[A lamp](#lit:2,5) turns evenly and throws [twelve flashes](#lit:6-17), 15° apart. Each lands at α + β·tan θ: α the [foot of the lamp](#lit:3), β its distance out.\n\n**The angles were laid by the turn before anything landed**: the marks are the lamp's addresses carried onto the sand."},{"title":"Half within one lamp-distance","text":"Half the turn lies [within 45° of the perpendicular](#lit:18-20), so **half the marks land within β of the foot**. [Their law](#lit:21), drawn under the shore from its formula, is the Cauchy.\n\nFind the lamp by the marks' median, never their mean: the far flashes run off toward the shore's ends. [The lighthouse, §1](https://github.com/reportbase/wander/blob/main/papers/essays/07-where-it-shows-up.md)"},{"title":"Drawn with the shore stretched","text":"Draw the shore at twice the sea's scale, *c* = 2, and the halfway flash is seen at 63.4°: **[the corner](#lit:19,20) slides off.** Drag *c* and watch [the count within β](#lit:6-17) leave six.\n\nOnly at *c* = 1, one length, is the turn still a turn. The lamp never holds a *c*; the stretch is the drawing's."},{"title":"Mercator's chart keeps the bearings","text":"Open the globe into Mercator's chart and [the rhumb line](#lit:35), a spiral on the globe, is straight: **a step north is drawn at the scale of a step east**, *c* = 1, everywhere.\n\nIt pays in area: [Greenland](#lit:33) swells about ten times. Bearings are directions; areas are amounts. [Mercator's chart, §2](https://github.com/reportbase/wander/blob/main/papers/essays/07-where-it-shows-up.md)"},{"title":"A moving sky","text":"Move through the stars and two things change. **Where each is seen moves** (aberration, a map of [the directions](#lit:41-52)); **what arrives changes** (the Doppler factor, drawn here as size).\n\nThe brightening ahead, *D*⁴, is *D*² of directions crowding and *D*² of what arrives. [A moving sky, §7](https://github.com/reportbase/wander/blob/main/papers/essays/07-where-it-shows-up.md)"},{"title":"Three pictures, one split","text":"The [lamp's angles](#lit:6-17), the [chart's bearings](#lit:35), the [sky's directions](#lit:41-52) are where things are seen, unmoved by scaling the world. The paces, the areas, the light are amounts, written in a unit someone carried in.\n\nPractice already keeps them apart. [Readers and Writers, §3](https://github.com/reportbase/wander/blob/main/papers/readers-and-writers.md)"}],"path":null,"items":[{"fill":{"color":"#f4f1ea","opacity":1},"stroke":null,"width":0,"open":false,"exact":{"x":[-0.9,0.9,0.9,-0.9],"y":[0.440816327,0.440816327,-0.440816327,-0.440816327],"r":null,"smooth":null,"ctrl":null,"holes":[]}},{"morph":0},{"morph":1},{"morph":18},{"morph":3},{"morph":5},{"morph":2},{"morph":6},{"morph":7},{"morph":8},{"morph":9},{"morph":10},{"morph":11},{"morph":12},{"morph":13},{"morph":14},{"morph":15},{"morph":16},{"morph":17},{"morph":19},{"morph":20},{"morph":21},{"morph